Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: stage stock ADSP for TB522FU battery telemetry

The USB-only probe left ADSP disabled, so qcom_battmgr never receives a
service-up event and every property returns EAGAIN. Enable the existing
SoC PAS path with board-scoped stock firmware. Keep audio and compute
clients disabled while battery/charging behavior is evaluated.

The existing 86 MiB ADSP carveout and 512 KiB configuration region match
the captured stock runtime tree. Both split MDT images pass segment and
manifest checks; firmware is supplied privately, never included here.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
@@ -592,3 +592,19 @@
 		serial0 = &uart15;
 	};
 };
+
+/* Stage the stock ADSP battery service. Its 86 MiB image and 512 KiB
+ * configuration carveouts match the captured runtime tree. Keep all firmware
+ * private and board-scoped; DSP audio/compute clients are separate bring-up.
+ * The disk-test profile blocks automatic PAS loading until USB/return checks.
+ */
+&remoteproc_adsp {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8750/lenovo/tb522fu/adsp.mdt",
+			"qcom/sm8750/lenovo/tb522fu/adsp_dtb.mdt";
+	status = "okay";
+
+	glink-edge {
+		fastrpc { status = "disabled"; };
+		gpr { status = "disabled"; };
+	};
+};
